138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (This recording captures a remembered commute from home to university during study abroad life. It follows the changing sound environment of the journey, from the quietness of leaving home to the rhythm of stations, trains and campus arrival. The piece represents one of the most familiar sound fragments of student life abroad.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (These sounds were chosen because commuting is an ordinary yet memorable part of study abroad life. Although the journey may feel routine at the time, the sounds of footsteps, waiting, announcements and train movement often remain in memory long after the experience has passed. This recording turns a daily routine into a lasting sonic memory.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (The artistic aim of this piece is to recreate the emotional rhythm of commuting as it might be remembered in the future. The recording should allow listeners to feel the transition from private space to public space, while reflecting the repetition, movement and atmosphere of everyday student life abroad. Rather than simple documentation, it is designed as a nostalgic fragment of lived experience.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
